  -- HONEST READ --
    A FIRST VERSION of this diagnostic (ESS on sign*gamma weights) was mathematically guaranteed to report 16.00/16 for every group, because gamma is constant per group in this project's PEC implementation -- that was a broken diagnostic, not a clean result, caught by inspecting raw entries before trusting it.
    The corrected version: 27/756 (3.6%) of (slot,label) groups have |mean_sign| < 0.5 across their 16 real draws -- i.e. the correction for these groups is closer to a coin flip than a confident signal, even before gamma amplifies whatever that noise is. This is a real, previously undiagnosed, concrete source of the pipeline's known instability (Task 32B's dominant PEC-MC variance, Task 33C's erratic per-k results): with only 16 draws, any group whose true sign-balance is genuinely close to 50/50 will have a highly unstable average, and gamma multiplies that noise directly into the final energy. This is a real, different, and probably more useful lever than Task 33B/33C's per-label damping: for groups with high noise_contribution, MORE real draws (not damping) would directly reduce sign_se (which shrinks as 1/sqrt(n)) -- a concrete, targeted (not blanket) case for extending N_MC beyond 16, but only for the specific high-noise groups identified above, not uniformly.

